00:04:48.888 --> 00:04:49.789
But when the government

00:04:49.789 --> 00:04:50.757
takes the extra money

00:04:50.757 --> 00:04:52.292
to provide the additional services

00:04:52.292 --> 00:04:54.794
that we need we go crazy about this.

00:04:55.228 --> 00:04:57.330
To me it's it is it's a double standard.

00:04:57.797 --> 00:05:00.900
What do you believe is a fair

00:05:01.467 --> 00:05:03.870
tax rate for the rich

00:05:06.105 --> 00:05:06.339
Well,

00:05:06.339 --> 00:05:08.708
that's a very convoluted question

00:05:08.708 --> 00:05:09.509
because are you

00:05:09.509 --> 00:05:10.877
are you talking about income

00:05:10.877 --> 00:05:13.179
or you're talking about assets?

00:05:13.713 --> 00:05:15.114
I really think we should go back

00:05:15.114 --> 00:05:16.115
to the same tax form

00:05:16.115 --> 00:05:17.150
that we had in the sixties

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:18.117
and the early seventies up

00:05:18.117 --> 00:05:19.752
until 1973,

00:05:19.752 --> 00:05:21.888
to go back to a progressive tax rate

00:05:21.888 --> 00:05:22.555
where the where

00:05:22.555 --> 00:05:26.259
the highest rate of taxes on on anybody

00:05:26.259 --> 00:05:26.859
and obviously

00:05:26.859 --> 00:05:27.660
the wealthy

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:29.762
gets all the way up to a 90% level.

00:05:30.096 --> 00:05:32.198
That's not $0.90 on the first dollars,

00:05:32.198 --> 00:05:34.167
not $0.90 on the first million.

00:05:34.167 --> 00:05:35.668
It escalates up to.

00:05:35.668 --> 00:05:37.837
